MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_001: Ha ha ha! This is good fun! Come now!\nHave another drink!
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_002: Hehe. You seem pretty well traveled. C'mon! Tell me\nmore of your stories!
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_003: Yang Jie seems to be in high spirits.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_004: He's one of the people I must protect as Mediator.\nIt's good to see he's having a nice time.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_005: Ah, yes. I know just the story to share! OK, so\nthere's this ancient weapon. They call it the Star.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_006: Oh no...
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_007: Yeah? Never heard of it, but it sounds interesting!
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_008: Its existence is highly secret. Even mentioning it\nbreaks the law of the forbidden land, some say.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_009: He's openly blabbing about the law! I have to step in.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_010: Yang Jie. I think you've had one too many. Let's go.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_011: Hm? Eh, alright. I see what you're doing here. Hey,\nno need to get pushy now.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_012: You were speaking far too freely back there. I can't\nbelieve you even started talking about Artemis.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_013: What if a spy from the temples overheard you? They\nmight even start monitoring you.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_014: We never know who's listening. Even now, there are\nthose within the temples who think of us as enemies.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_015: Our fate is but the gods' design. What will be, will be.\nDid you know I once served as a priest?
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_016: Despite being a descendant from the People of the\nWhite Egg?
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_017: Why should that matter? I have never been bound\nto any one place.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_018: I am a wanderer. I have traversed lands east of\nNormalia—the distant land of Sai!
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_019: You are indeed strange... Everything about you runs\ncounter to what I know.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_020: You must abandon such narrow thinking. There are\nmany things in this world one could never imagine.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_021: Rules and regulations are often trivial. They serve to\nbind our minds, but you must break free, Anatolia.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_022: I don't consider rules to be "trivial." No, they're\nnecessary!
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_023: Getting drunk and leaking sensitive information is\nunacceptable. So please, watch yourself.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_024: Indeed. It is true that alcohol has a way of loosening\none's tongue. Such is human nature.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_025: However, my conversation partner was similarly\ninebriated. He won't remember what transpired.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_C_026: If you don't adjust your attitude, then I have no\nchoice but to monitor you myself.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_001: Thank you so much for everything. If you hadn't\ncome, I don't know what would've happened.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_002: Yeah, thank you! Thank you! Thanks for chasing\noff the scary people!
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_003: It was my honor. Take care now.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_004: You did a great job back there. I'm relieved they're\nboth safe.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_005: It surprised me to see you acting the role of a knight.\nYou were very convincing.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_006: Asserting one's authority is enough to spook most\nruffians. My goal was to avoid violence.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_007: While serving as a priest, I befriended many knights.\nCopying their manner of speech can be quite useful.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_008: You have a lot of knowledge and experience, and I\nsee you use it to your advantage.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_009: I'm sure you've saved many lives that way. This is a\nside of you I've never seen before.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_010: I have enjoyed learning more about you too,\nespecially given our shared background.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_011: Oh, you've wanted to get to know me? How would\nthat be advantageous for you?
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_012: Of course I've been curious. Who wouldn't want to\nknow more about the being created to save Kunlun?
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_013: I often wondered what shape it might take. The\nlife-form made to save the Demon's Land.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_014: Is that what you call it? That's an interesting choice\nof words...
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_015: My grandfather told me time and again of Kunlun's\nplight, and of the Mediator who betrayed them.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_016: But after observing you, I was...surprised. You are\nso earnest. So sincere.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_017: I never realized you were monitoring me as well...\nYou're certainly cunning.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_018: Heh heh. I do have my moments.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_019: Hmmm... Maybe your blabbing about secrets was\nan act, after all.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_020: You saw me, and then you acted in a way that might\ndraw my attention.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_021: I do recall the man you were talking to was drunk...
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_022: He'd either have forgotten your mention of the\nStar or he'd have thought it a joke.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_023: Ultimately there was no real risk, even though you\nspoke of multiple secrets.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_024: You must have figured that the benefit of monitoring\nme would be greater than any perceived risk.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_025: You are a true Mediator. And a smart one at that.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_026: Smart enough to recognize your own sharpness and\nadaptability.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_027: Well, to be honest, it was all coincidental. I only\nmentioned the Star to liven up the drinking party.
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_028: Are you serious?
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_029: You talked about it to "liven things up"?! That was\nthe reason?
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_030: A successful party needs both good booze and good\nconversation. Everything else is superfluous!
MID_SE_Anh_Yan_B_031: After all the time I spent monitoring you, I still don't\nunderstand you...